# A ball with a 2-limb center times a number a of the format: the center by mul_2_1, plus
# U |cz| + V from the claims of mul_2_1.
kernel:        ball_scale_2
input:         cx = cx0 cx1
input:         rx
input:         a
output:        cz = cz0 cz1
output:        rz
value:         cx*a
requires:      normalized cx
requires:      nonneg rx
ensures:       normalized cz
ensures:       encloses cz rz x*a x=cx,rx
min_precision: 2
source:        midpoint-radius scaling (Milestone 1 listing)
status:        unverified
cone_exempt:   the radius never reaches the center; the special states of the ball layer (Milestone 1 statements, Ball kernels) test the center and the radii

(cz0, cz1) = mul_2_1(cx0, cx1, a)
aa         = abs(a)
t1         = rmul(aa, rx)
mz         = abs_upper_2(cz0, cz1)
d0         = rmul(const unit_computed(mul_2_1), mz)
d          = radd(d0, const tiny_computed(mul_2_1))
rz         = radd(t1, d)
